mapping "W6598.1" source="W6598" target="220987009" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 1 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence-unassessable@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source W6598 (Swedish ICD-10 5-char extension of W65 SNOMED CT 220987009, activity = other
        specified) encodes the clinical event of bathtub drowning plus an activity modifier. Target
        SNOMED CT 40417698 (concept_code 220987009) = [X]Drowning and submersion while in bath-tub (place
        unspecified). The target captures the same clinical drowning event; it drops the source's
        activity-axis qualifier, which has no SNOMED CT analogue (it is an external-cause epidemiological
        modifier, not a clinical feature). Broader because the target fully contains the clinical event;
        the dropped activity is metadata outside the target's scope. Moderate tier: the W65 parent maps
        to SNOMED CT via Athena crosswalk (W65 -> 436592), and the SNOMED CT [X] concept is a closer
        ICD-10-aligned equivalent, but the Swedish 5-char extension has no direct crosswalk and adds an
        unmapped activity axis.
        """
}
mapping "W6599.1" source="W6599" target="220987009" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 1 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence-unassessable@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source W6599 (Swedish ICD-10 5-char extension of W65 SNOMED CT 220987009, activity = unspecified)
        encodes the clinical event of bathtub drowning plus an unspecified activity modifier. Target
        SNOMED CT 40417698 (concept_code 220987009) = [X]Drowning and submersion while in bath-tub (place
        unspecified). The target captures the same clinical drowning event; the activity axis is not
        represented in SNOMED CT. Broader: target fully contains the clinical event; the unspecified
        activity is metadata. Moderate tier: W65 Athena crosswalk exists to 436592; the [X] SNOMED CT
        concept is the ICD-10-aligned equivalent but the Swedish 5-char extension has no direct
        crosswalk.
        """
}
